I posted one reply this session: on #1097, which I then closed. I skipped every other issue on the list.

• #1097 (closed): commit d0e76d77 fixes it. Each /spawn worker now holds an exclusive lock on a .lock file that sits beside its worktree. The stale sweep won't remove a worktree whose lock another process holds, and the OS drops the lock when that process dies. I read the commit message before commenting. That's where the test results and the check that the test fails when the lock check is disabled come from; I didn't re-run them myself. The comment also says two things are still open: network filesystems are unmeasured, and on a platform where the lock can't be taken a worker runs unprotected, as before the fix.
